grml.agent boots GRML, provides an interactive host-side Tmux REPL,
and can build custom live ISOs using grml-live.

Usage:
  grml.agent boot [PROFILE_NAME] [--verify-deb-cache] [--iso PATH]
  grml.agent tmux [--iso PATH]
  grml.agent prepare_alpine_bundle [alpine_branch]
  grml.agent --help
  grml.agent --version

Package profiles:
  shared/profiles/PROFILE_NAME/packages.txt
    Optional Debian packages installed into the running GRML guest by boot
    or apply_profile. One package name per line; blank lines and # comments
    are ignored. Applying another profile does not uninstall packages.

grml-live build profiles:
  shared/profiles/PROFILE_NAME/builder-packages.txt
    Optional extra Debian packages installed into the guest that runs grml-live.
  shared/profiles/PROFILE_NAME/grml-live/build.yml
    YAML manifest containing the suite, classes, system identity, boot options,
    Secure Boot setting, Debian wayback snapshot date, grml-live git ref, and
    other build options.
  shared/profiles/PROFILE_NAME/grml-live/config/
    Class-based configuration overlays merged over upstream grml-live/config.
    Use package_config/CLASS for ISO package selection, bootstrap-keyring/CLASS
    for mmdebstrap signing keys, and debconf/, env/, files/, hooks/, scripts/,
    media-files/, media-scripts/, and tools/ for build-time customization.
    The grml/ directory holds global grml-live settings. Filesystem overlays
    preserve symbolic links for system configuration.
  shared/profiles/PROFILE_NAME/grml-live/chroot-install/
    Optional directory copied under / in the build chroot.

Host REPL workflow:
  prepare_build_environment PROFILE_NAME
    Install grml-live prerequisites, configure the unprivileged build account
    and user namespaces, and check out the grml-live revision from build.yml.
  validate_profile PROFILE_NAME
    Validate build.yml, builder package names, custom class definitions, and
    the profile file tree.
  build_iso PROFILE_NAME
    Run grml-live image-create and preserve the ISO and logs in
    /mnt/shared/grml-live/runs/PROFILE_NAME/RUN_ID/output/.

grml-live requires an unprivileged user with working user namespaces and
subordinate UID/GID ranges. grml.agent creates a dedicated grml-live-builder
account. Build temporary files stay under /var/tmp; output is copied to the
shared directory after the build. Select only profiles and scripts you trust.

Other host REPL commands:
  ocr
    Recognize text in the latest captured guest display frame.
  guest_exec <shell command>
    Execute a shell command inside the GRML guest through QEMU Guest Agent.
    Output and exit status are returned to the host REPL. Commands run as root.
  apply_profile PROFILE_NAME
    Install or update packages from packages.txt into the running guest.
  prepare_alpine_bundle [alpine_branch]
    Prepare and verify an offline Alpine APK repository bundle.
  prepare_deb_cache
    Configure apt-cacher-ng to cache Debian package downloads.
  verify_deb_cache [package]
    Verify that a package archive can be fetched while upstream access is disabled.
  create_disk <name> <size> [qcow2|raw]
    Create and hot-attach a disk image under ./disks/.
  attach_disk <path> [qcow2|raw]
    Hot-attach an existing disk image.
  create_ext4_disk <name> <size> [mountpoint] [qcow2|raw]
    Create, partition, format, and mount a new ext4 disk in the guest.

Logging:
  GRML_AGENT_REPL_FOCUS=true|false (default: true)
  XEPHYR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO|DEBUG|TRACE (default: INFO)
